You are implementing features for a Blazor Web App shipment tracker at `/tmp/sv-f385aa52a7214aeaa089390769c6e46d/ShipmentTracker`. The project uses Interactive Auto Global mode with Individual authentication. It has two projects:
- `ShipmentTracker` (server) 
- `ShipmentTracker.Client` (WebAssembly client)

## Requirements
- Dispatchers view a list of shipments with status and destination
- Customers check their shipment status and estimated delivery
- Authentication with individual accounts (already scaffolded)

## Architecture (Auto mode)
- Interactive components MUST be in the `.Client` project
- Data access from client components must go through HTTP APIs
- Define interfaces in `.Client`, implement with HttpClient there, implement with EF Core on server
- Both Program.cs files must register matching services

