You are implementing features for a Blazor Web App shipment tracker at `/tmp/sv-f385aa52a7214aeaa089390769c6e46d/ShipmentTracker`. The project uses Interactive Auto Global mode with Individual authentication. It has two projects:
- `ShipmentTracker` (server) 
- `ShipmentTracker.Client` (WebAssembly client)

## Requirements
- Dispatchers view a list of shipments with status and destination
- Customers check their shipment status and estimated delivery
- Authentication with individual accounts (already scaffolded)

## Architecture (Auto mode)
- Interactive components MUST be in the `.Client` project
- Data access from client components must go through HTTP APIs
- Define interfaces in `.Client`, implement with HttpClient there, implement with EF Core on server
- Both Program.cs files must register matching services

## Tasks

### 1. Create shared model in Client project

Create `/tmp/sv-f385aa52a7214aeaa089390769c6e46d/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed
}
```

### 2. Create IShipmentService interface in Client project

Create `/tmp/sv-f385aa52a7214aeaa089390769c6e46d/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string email);
    Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment);
    Task<Shipment> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status);
}
```

### 3. Create client-side HttpClient implementation

Create `/tmp/sv-f385aa52a7214aeaa089390769c6e46d/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentHttpService : IShipmentService
{
    private readonly HttpClient _http;

    public ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient http)
    {
        _http = http;
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await _http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        return await _http.GetFromJsonAsync<Shipment?>($"api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string email)
    {
        return await _http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>($"api/shipments/customer/{Uri.EscapeDataString(email)}") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment)
    {
        var response = await _http.PostAsJsonAsync("api/shipments", shipment);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>() ?? shipment;
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        var response = await _http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", status);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>() ?? new Shipment { Id = id, Status = status };
    }
}
```

### 4. Register HttpClient and service in Client Program.cs

Edit `/tmp/sv-f385aa52a7214aeaa089390769c6e46d/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Program.cs` to:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

